      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Companies that try to remain strictly apolitical are already failing because they are not truly serving their customers' values. In the modern era, consumers view corporate silence on major social issues as a political endorsement of the status quo, which is often the opposing side. Your brand identity *is* political, and by supporting the reform, you are aligning yourself with the progressive values that drive your most engaged market.",
      "source": "target",
